      "provenance": {
        "notes": "One fetched page only. SDSU says people and pets should not eat it; the pet-specific severity, agents and symptoms are the agent's. Habit 'rosette' is a mapping from 'leaves fanning from the centre'. Interval: NC State 'allow soil to completely dry between waterings', less often in winter; Missouri Botanical Garden 'water very moderately in spring, summer and fall, reduce to a minimum in winter'. No days given; completely dry in a 13 cm clay-type pot takes about two weeks, so 14. Plastic pots would run longer. Pot and season: 13 cm pot, bright indirect light, room temperature, growing season. Dry and wet tolerance days: no source gives days, left as before (from_knowledge_verify)."
